# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A macro name carries the characters the host's own name regexp admits"

# TiddlyWiki reads a macro name with /([^\s>"'=]+)/y — parseMacroInvocationAsTransclusion
# in core/modules/parsers/parseutils.js. Quote and equals END the name, a colon reads through
# it (TiddlyWiki5 #10015), and a name of zero characters fails the call outright.
#
# Every negative below stands beside a positive at the same column, so a column that stopped
# naming anything fails loudly rather than passing empty. Every column here comes off a
# snapshot of these same lines, never off a hand count.

! A name of ordinary letters reads to its end

x <<myMacro>> y
# ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.procedurecallinline.begin.tiddlywiki5
#   ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.procedure.tiddlywiki5
#         ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.procedure.tiddlywiki5
#          ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.procedurecallinline.end.tiddlywiki5

! A colon reads through the name, so the call names the whole run

x <<a:b>> y
#   ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.procedure.tiddlywiki5
#    ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.procedure.tiddlywiki5
#     ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.procedure.tiddlywiki5
#      ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.procedurecallinline.end.tiddlywiki5

A system title reads as one name, never a `$` and a positional value:

x <<$:/a/b>> y
#   ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.procedure.tiddlywiki5
#    ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.procedure.tiddlywiki5
#        ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.procedure.tiddlywiki5
#    ^ - meta.variable.procedure.parameters.tiddlywiki5

! An equals sign ends the name the same way

x <<a=b>> y
#   ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.procedure.tiddlywiki5
#    ^ - variable.name.procedure.tiddlywiki5
#    ^ meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedure.parameters.tiddlywiki5

! A colon alone names a call

# The fr-FR edition writes this as prose about camel case. A colon reads as a name character, so
# TiddlyWiki builds a call on the variable `:` here, between the prose on either side.
NDT<<:>> here
#  ^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.procedurecallinline.begin.tiddlywiki5
#    ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.procedure.tiddlywiki5
#     ^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.procedurecallinline.end.tiddlywiki5

! A call carrying no name at all opens nothing

# A name of zero characters fails the call, and the brackets fall back to the prose around them.
NDT<<>> here
#  ^ - punctuation.definition.procedurecallinline.begin.tiddlywiki5
#  ^ - meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5
#    ^ - variable.name.procedure.tiddlywiki5
#    ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5
